1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:04,285
The money from Congressman
Ramon dela Peña's illegal businesses

2
00:00:04,285 --> 00:00:06,351
is being laundered in Casa Fuerte.

3
00:00:06,351 --> 00:00:08,509
Stay here until the situation becomes okay.

4
00:00:08,509 --> 00:00:10,510
- Why did you have to drag me into it?
- The kid asked for your help

5
00:00:10,510 --> 00:00:12,559
while he was having a heart attack.
But what did you do?

6
00:00:12,559 --> 00:00:16,883
- Where's the typewriter?
- How does the darn typewriter work?

7
00:00:16,883 --> 00:00:18,879
You can change your life!

8
00:00:18,879 --> 00:00:21,121
I know how much you loved me.

9
00:00:21,121 --> 00:00:23,715
You got my father blind.
What should I do with it?

10
00:00:23,715 --> 00:00:25,074
Who told you that?

11
00:00:25,074 --> 00:00:26,699
No secret remains hidden forever.

12
00:00:26,699 --> 00:00:29,129
I will kill Liam.

13
00:00:29,129 --> 00:00:30,531
No, Dad! Please.

14
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:32,298
Dad, please! Not Liam!

15
00:00:32,298 --> 00:00:34,601
- Dad!
- He was brought to Pulang Buhangin.

16
00:00:34,601 --> 00:00:38,270
Liam was abducted.

17
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,422
I treated you like my son.

18
00:00:56,389 --> 00:00:59,228
You gave me hope.

19
00:01:00,837 --> 00:01:05,665
I even forgot that
I was grieving for my wife

20
00:01:05,665 --> 00:01:10,269
because you brought me success.

21
00:01:19,457 --> 00:01:22,216
I trusted you...

22
00:01:23,297 --> 00:01:27,091
because I could see myself in you.

23
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:33,194
But you're a traitor!

24
00:01:39,261 --> 00:01:41,913
I raised a monster.

25
00:01:44,237 --> 00:01:50,415
I didn't know that
you'd bite the hand that feeds you.

26
00:01:57,417 --> 00:02:00,120
You don't have an ounce of conscience!

27
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,621
Go on and shoot.

28
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:03,672
Shoot me!

29
00:02:04,477 --> 00:02:05,792
What?

30
00:02:05,792 --> 00:02:07,861
Kill me!

31
00:02:26,779 --> 00:02:29,282
You're evil!

32
00:02:29,282 --> 00:02:31,317
You should die!

33
00:02:31,317 --> 00:02:33,502
You are all talk.

34
00:02:34,688 --> 00:02:36,723
You know me.

35
00:02:36,723 --> 00:02:40,279
My life, my game.

36
00:02:41,695 --> 00:02:44,765
So why don't we play?

37
00:02:44,765 --> 00:02:47,201
Survival of the fittest.

38
00:02:47,201 --> 00:02:50,370
Both our lives are worthless anyway.

39
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:54,000
Let's see who will get lucky.

40
00:02:55,399 --> 00:02:58,519
Let the bullet judge...

41
00:03:01,348 --> 00:03:04,144
who should stay alive.

42
00:03:08,222 --> 00:03:12,226
Until now, you still want to be in control.

43
00:03:12,226 --> 00:03:15,462
You treat everyone like puppets!

44
00:03:27,808 --> 00:03:31,712
Were you even a good father to Via?

45
00:03:31,712 --> 00:03:34,915
I'm not surprised that
your daughter became evil!

46
00:03:34,915 --> 00:03:37,484
You're a worthless father!

47
00:03:37,484 --> 00:03:39,653
It's too late for the sermon.

48
00:03:39,653 --> 00:03:42,256
I already lost a lot.

49
00:03:42,256 --> 00:03:46,189
Now, I want you to get lost!

50
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,515
Are you serious, Lando?

51
00:04:09,515 --> 00:04:12,051
You brought a typewriter?

52
00:04:12,051 --> 00:04:13,753
Take it easy.

53
00:04:13,753 --> 00:04:15,688
I brought a gun too.

54
00:04:15,688 --> 00:04:19,989
Did you know that this typewriter is magical?

55
00:04:20,893 --> 00:04:24,563
Did you also know that I once died?

56
00:04:33,639 --> 00:04:38,669
But because of this, I came back to life.

57
00:04:39,745 --> 00:04:45,718
Via, did you know that
this thing can change your life?

58
00:04:45,718 --> 00:04:49,121
You can wish whatever you want.

59
00:04:49,121 --> 00:04:53,830
All you have to do is write it
using this typewriter.

60
00:05:02,501 --> 00:05:08,407
This story should have a magical typewriter.

61
00:05:08,407 --> 00:05:12,244
The hero will return to the past,

62
00:05:12,244 --> 00:05:17,111
and he will use the typewriter to do that.

63
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:39,605
I will never let you use me again!

64
00:05:39,605 --> 00:05:42,574
Your wickedness has to end!

65
00:05:43,309 --> 00:05:45,611
Okay, then.

66
00:05:45,611 --> 00:05:47,422
I'm setting you free.

67
00:05:54,954 --> 00:05:56,489
Go on.

68
00:05:56,489 --> 00:05:59,492
Go ahead! Kill me!

69
00:05:59,492 --> 00:06:02,628
I'm not scared of you! I'm not scared to die!

70
00:06:02,628 --> 00:06:04,720
Kill me now!

71
00:06:06,565 --> 00:06:08,486
Dad!

72
00:07:46,499 --> 00:07:49,134
Liam, Liam.

73
00:07:49,134 --> 00:07:50,903
Liam, Liam...

74
00:07:50,903 --> 00:07:52,238
Liam, wake up. Wake up!

75
00:07:52,238 --> 00:07:54,856
Don't be like this. Please, please.

76
00:07:59,011 --> 00:08:01,480
Liam, Liam!

77
00:08:02,414 --> 00:08:03,916
Liam.

78
00:08:03,916 --> 00:08:05,951
Love...

79
00:08:05,951 --> 00:08:07,419
I'm so sorry, my love.

80
00:08:07,419 --> 00:08:10,588
I'm so sorry.

81
00:08:11,457 --> 00:08:13,526
I'm so sorry, my love.

82
00:08:13,526 --> 00:08:14,994
Liam, my love.

83
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:16,762
Love!

84
00:08:16,762 --> 00:08:18,330
Love!

85
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:20,632
Love!

86
00:08:21,267 --> 00:08:22,601
Help!

87
00:08:22,601 --> 00:08:25,104
Help!

88
00:08:25,104 --> 00:08:27,273
Help! Please, help us!

89
00:08:27,273 --> 00:08:29,608
Love...

90
00:08:29,608 --> 00:08:33,311
Liam!

91
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:37,659
No, no, no, no, no.

92
00:09:03,842 --> 00:09:07,313
If you really are magical...

93
00:09:07,313 --> 00:09:09,371
then show me.

94
00:09:10,849 --> 00:09:13,485
<i>I love you so much, Liam.</i>

95
00:09:13,485 --> 00:09:16,322
<i>You are my life.</i>

96
00:09:16,322 --> 00:09:19,925
<i>I will die if I lose you.</i>

97
00:09:19,925 --> 00:09:24,195
<i>If I have to take you away from death,
I will.</i>

98
00:09:24,863 --> 00:09:27,738
<i>You're only mine, Liam.</i>

99
00:09:30,202 --> 00:09:32,995
What did you do, Via?

100
00:09:36,609 --> 00:09:38,331
Joyce...

101
00:09:51,690 --> 00:09:55,194
<i>I won't let my dad kill you.</i>

102
00:09:55,194 --> 00:09:58,364
<i>I will catch the bullet for you.</i>

103
00:09:58,364 --> 00:10:00,865
<i>We will be together.</i>

104
00:10:02,201 --> 00:10:04,350
<i>This is what I want.</i>

105
00:10:06,305 --> 00:10:08,420
<i>This is my wish.</i>

106
00:10:21,487 --> 00:10:23,922
<i>Where am I?</i>

107
00:10:24,757 --> 00:10:28,126
<i>What's this? Is this another dream?</i>

108
00:10:57,189 --> 00:10:59,158
<i>So, what if she doesn't like me?</i>

109
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:01,360
<i>What if she does?</i>

110
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,328
<i>Take a leap of faith.</i>

111
00:11:03,328 --> 00:11:04,619
<i>I love you.</i>

112
00:11:04,619 --> 00:11:08,233
<i>You're supposed to pick Dexter up!
Where were you?</i>

113
00:11:10,436 --> 00:11:13,578
Liam was telling the truth.

114
00:11:14,969 --> 00:11:19,676
The typewriter is truly magical.
We did have a life together.

115
00:11:19,676 --> 00:11:21,277
Joyce, please forgive me.

116
00:11:21,277 --> 00:11:23,246
It is all my fault.

117
00:11:23,246 --> 00:11:26,683
I didn't mean it, Joyce. Please, forgive me.

118
00:11:26,683 --> 00:11:30,858
Liam, what are you doing?
What are you talking about?

119
00:11:35,758 --> 00:11:37,600
What's happening?

120
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:45,777
Liam?

121
00:11:51,808 --> 00:11:54,074
Dex!

122
00:12:02,652 --> 00:12:07,623
<i>For the third time,
your story will change, Liam...</i>

123
00:12:07,623 --> 00:12:09,959
<i>And even those who are dear to you.</i>

124
00:12:09,959 --> 00:12:11,127
<i>This is not what you wanted.</i>

125
00:12:11,127 --> 00:12:13,759
<i>So brace yourself
for what can happen in return.</i>

126
00:12:18,601 --> 00:12:20,548
Where am I?

127
00:12:21,464 --> 00:12:23,205
Where are we?

128
00:12:25,884 --> 00:12:27,447
<i>I won't let my Dad kill you.</i>

129
00:12:27,447 --> 00:12:29,017
Via.

130
00:12:29,017 --> 00:12:30,269
Via! Via!

131
00:12:30,269 --> 00:12:33,120
<i>I will take the bullet for you.</i>

132
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:35,589
Via. Via.

133
00:12:35,589 --> 00:12:38,125
<i>We'll be together.</i>

134
00:12:38,125 --> 00:12:40,515
Via, Via, why?

135
00:12:41,996 --> 00:12:43,497
Why not?

136
00:12:43,497 --> 00:12:45,833
<i>This is what I want.</i>

137
00:12:45,833 --> 00:12:47,368
<i>This is my wish.</i>

138
00:12:47,368 --> 00:12:49,269
I love you, Liam.

139
00:12:49,269 --> 00:12:52,840
Via, don't talk like that.

140
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:55,175
Via, Via, Via.

141
00:12:55,175 --> 00:12:56,710
Via.

142
00:12:56,710 --> 00:12:59,384
Via, Via, Via, Via.

143
00:12:59,384 --> 00:13:02,950
Via, Via, Via, Via.

144
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:04,634
Via?

145
00:13:07,655 --> 00:13:10,024
Lando.

146
00:13:10,024 --> 00:13:12,696
What are you and Via doing here?

147
00:13:17,364 --> 00:13:20,634
That bullet was supposed to be for you.

148
00:13:20,634 --> 00:13:23,037
Lando!

149
00:13:23,037 --> 00:13:24,966
Get Via.

150
00:13:27,374 --> 00:13:29,343
Sir...

151
00:13:29,343 --> 00:13:34,348
I'm sorry, but this is already out of hand.

152
00:13:34,348 --> 00:13:35,983
That's your daughter.

153
00:13:35,983 --> 00:13:38,218
I don't want to get involved.

154
00:13:41,689 --> 00:13:44,170
You're already worthless.

155
00:14:02,142 --> 00:14:06,366
Via, I remember I rushed you to the hospital.

156
00:14:08,515 --> 00:14:11,960
You also collapsed in the hospital.

157
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:16,006
What my dad did to you was really bad.

158
00:14:17,858 --> 00:14:20,360
But thank you, Liam.

159
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,738
Thank you for saving me.

160
00:14:23,864 --> 00:14:25,698
If it wasn't for you...

161
00:14:27,703 --> 00:14:30,486
it would have been worse.

162
00:14:33,874 --> 00:14:36,994
The doctor told me I could no longer walk.

163
00:14:39,079 --> 00:14:42,275
Why did you take the bullet for me?

164
00:14:44,451 --> 00:14:47,494
After what I did to you, Via?

165
00:14:50,457 --> 00:14:52,424
I don't know, either.

166
00:14:54,595 --> 00:14:56,927
When we were there...

167
00:14:58,132 --> 00:15:03,787
I wasn't thinking about
the painful events.

168
00:15:06,272 --> 00:15:08,318
All I know is...

169
00:15:09,681 --> 00:15:11,481
I love you.

170
00:15:14,615 --> 00:15:16,178
Liam...

171
00:15:18,118 --> 00:15:20,525
Liam, I still love you.

172
00:15:27,795 --> 00:15:30,030
Don't worry.

173
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:32,050
We're safe here.

174
00:15:32,933 --> 00:15:35,792
I asked Queenie for help.

175
00:15:37,947 --> 00:15:42,175
We're in her house in the province.

176
00:15:44,011 --> 00:15:47,014
I need to take you away from my dad.

177
00:15:47,014 --> 00:15:49,650
We need to hide.

178
00:15:49,650 --> 00:15:52,686
I'm sorry, Via.

179
00:15:52,686 --> 00:15:58,491
I know what Ramon can do to get back at me.

180
00:16:01,662 --> 00:16:06,932
I only want to make sure
that my loved ones are safe.

181
00:16:09,536 --> 00:16:11,672
I need to see them.

182
00:16:11,672 --> 00:16:13,574
Liam.

183
00:16:13,574 --> 00:16:15,911
Aunt Tess is safe.

184
00:16:17,544 --> 00:16:19,341
And Joyce too.

185
00:16:21,802 --> 00:16:23,575
How did you know?

186
00:16:27,721 --> 00:16:31,391
Queenie is monitoring them,

187
00:16:31,391 --> 00:16:35,069
and she keeps me updated
every chance she gets.

188
00:16:37,998 --> 00:16:41,668
Can you please believe me
just this once, Liam?

189
00:16:41,668 --> 00:16:43,916
Trust me.

190
00:16:50,944 --> 00:16:54,455
When you chose Joyce over me,

191
00:16:55,582 --> 00:16:57,372
I knew...

192
00:16:59,753 --> 00:17:03,400
I could no longer decide for you.

193
00:17:07,728 --> 00:17:10,611
The doors are not locked, Liam.

194
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:13,525
You can leave.

195
00:17:16,270 --> 00:17:20,040
But you said it yourself.

196
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:23,300
You know what my dad can do.

197
00:17:24,978 --> 00:17:28,375
He won't stop as long as he's free.

198
00:17:34,588 --> 00:17:38,594
I only want them to be safe, Via.

199
00:17:39,826 --> 00:17:41,954
I won't leave.

200
00:17:42,996 --> 00:17:46,735
I won't also leave you in that condition.

201
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:52,305
Thank you.

202
00:18:07,399 --> 00:18:09,027
Joyce.

203
00:18:11,825 --> 00:18:13,461
Joyce.

204
00:18:15,295 --> 00:18:17,124
Liam...

205
00:18:21,034 --> 00:18:23,669
Liam is my husband.

206
00:18:30,177 --> 00:18:31,958
Dex...

207
00:18:34,881 --> 00:18:36,754
Dex, my son...

208
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:43,237
- My son.
- Joyce, Joyce.

209
00:18:45,993 --> 00:18:47,127
Joyce.

210
00:18:47,127 --> 00:18:48,195
Joyce...

211
00:18:54,368 --> 00:18:55,402
Joyce.

212
00:18:55,402 --> 00:18:56,703
Joyce.

213
00:18:56,703 --> 00:18:58,339
Liam...

214
00:19:05,712 --> 00:19:07,714
Joyce, you're awake now.
Joyce, you're already awake.

215
00:19:07,714 --> 00:19:09,916
Joyce, you're awake.

216
00:19:09,916 --> 00:19:11,818
I'm glad you're finally awake.

217
00:19:11,818 --> 00:19:14,375
Joyce, look at me.

218
00:19:15,389 --> 00:19:18,358
What's the last thing you remember?

219
00:19:18,358 --> 00:19:19,985
Because...

220
00:19:22,062 --> 00:19:25,699
when you left me at the coffee shop...

221
00:19:25,699 --> 00:19:28,164
we received a report.

222
00:19:29,336 --> 00:19:31,438
They saw you unconscious

223
00:19:31,438 --> 00:19:35,530
beside the lifeless body
of Lando Nakpil in a parking lot.

224
00:19:38,412 --> 00:19:40,015
Joyce...

225
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:44,030
what really happened?

226
00:19:48,789 --> 00:19:51,250
I confirmed everything that was happening
was all real.

227
00:19:51,250 --> 00:19:56,530
I had to confirm everything
before asking for your help.

228
00:19:56,530 --> 00:19:58,698
But it was too late when I got there, Hans.

229
00:19:58,698 --> 00:19:59,766
Because...

230
00:19:59,766 --> 00:20:04,104
Because Ramon was about to shoot Liam
but Via saved him.

231
00:20:04,104 --> 00:20:06,587
She took the bullet.

232
00:20:11,144 --> 00:20:15,115
Yes, they have a hospital record, but...

233
00:20:15,115 --> 00:20:18,785
after that, Liam and Via went missing.

234
00:20:18,785 --> 00:20:20,583
What?

235
00:20:21,755 --> 00:20:24,956
What do you mean they're missing?

236
00:20:26,626 --> 00:20:27,994
What's going on? Why are we here?

237
00:20:27,994 --> 00:20:30,797
We're like rats hiding in a hole.

238
00:20:30,797 --> 00:20:33,699
Why is this happening?

239
00:20:35,139 --> 00:20:38,171
I'm also not used to this look, Madam.

240
00:20:38,171 --> 00:20:41,967
It feels strange.

241
00:20:45,812 --> 00:20:50,584
Oh, come on! I even left my lipstick
because we were in a hurry.

242
00:20:50,584 --> 00:20:52,352
Oh.

243
00:20:52,352 --> 00:20:55,087
I'm glad I was able to bring this.

244
00:20:57,290 --> 00:20:59,426
Madam...

245
00:20:59,426 --> 00:21:01,461
The gold you are wearing might melt

246
00:21:01,461 --> 00:21:05,432
and turn you into an Oscars statuette
for Best Actress.

247
00:21:05,432 --> 00:21:07,801
Don't you feel the heat?

248
00:21:07,801 --> 00:21:09,336
You talk too much.

249
00:21:09,336 --> 00:21:11,204
Mind your own business.

250
00:21:11,204 --> 00:21:12,772
And look at this.

251
00:21:12,772 --> 00:21:14,608
This is my investment.

252
00:21:14,608 --> 00:21:16,109
I'm glad I brought it.

253
00:21:16,109 --> 00:21:20,313
They won't get stolen.

254
00:21:20,313 --> 00:21:25,719
Your mom is taking it out on me again.

255
00:21:25,719 --> 00:21:27,538
Mommy, please.

256
00:21:29,055 --> 00:21:31,958
What matters is that we're safe.

257
00:21:31,958 --> 00:21:34,361
Listen to your daughter, Joanne.

258
00:21:34,361 --> 00:21:35,462
Oh, wow.

259
00:21:35,462 --> 00:21:37,330
Are you ganging up on me?

260
00:21:37,330 --> 00:21:40,467
That's what you're good at.
Taking each other's sides.

261
00:21:40,467 --> 00:21:42,969
You're both stupid.

262
00:21:42,969 --> 00:21:46,473
You think we're safe
because we're in a safe house.

263
00:21:46,473 --> 00:21:50,710
But the truth is, we're in a safe house
because we're not safe!

264
00:21:50,710 --> 00:21:52,626
That's the truth!

265
00:21:53,605 --> 00:21:58,818
Madam, you better take off your jewelry.

266
00:21:58,818 --> 00:22:00,687
It reflects the sunlight.

267
00:22:00,687 --> 00:22:02,822
That's why you're getting
even more hot-headed.

268
00:22:02,822 --> 00:22:05,725
You shine like a disco ball at noon.

269
00:22:05,725 --> 00:22:07,494
There's a heatwave across the country.

270
00:22:07,494 --> 00:22:09,829
You might suffer from heat stroke.

271
00:22:09,829 --> 00:22:14,834
Complaining won't do us any good, Joanne.

272
00:22:14,834 --> 00:22:16,836
We'll stay here.

273
00:22:16,836 --> 00:22:20,708
No one is stopping you from leaving.

274
00:22:36,523 --> 00:22:37,995
- Hans.
- Auntie.

275
00:22:37,995 --> 00:22:41,366
Oh? What's the matter?

276
00:22:43,029 --> 00:22:47,191
Aunt Joanne wants to go out.

277
00:22:51,204 --> 00:22:55,117
Aunt, it's dangerous to go against someone
like Ramon dela Peña.

278
00:22:56,543 --> 00:23:01,748
So I hope you stay put.

279
00:23:01,748 --> 00:23:04,414
I don't want you to end up like Intoy.

280
00:23:05,385 --> 00:23:11,032
Luckily, we found him alive in your house.

281
00:23:13,727 --> 00:23:18,302
You know what, Hans,
I'm not only scared for us.

282
00:23:19,332 --> 00:23:21,270
I'm also scared for Liam.

283
00:23:22,569 --> 00:23:24,772
No mother can be at peace without knowing

284
00:23:24,772 --> 00:23:28,074
where her son could be or if he's safe.

285
00:23:28,074 --> 00:23:33,458
I'll make sure
that you'll reunite with your family.

286
00:23:34,514 --> 00:23:36,599
I promise you that.

287
00:23:38,652 --> 00:23:39,753
Thank you.

288
00:23:39,753 --> 00:23:41,919
Thank you, Hans.

289
00:23:44,124 --> 00:23:47,661
I'll leave you for now.
I also need to talk to the police.

290
00:23:47,661 --> 00:23:49,239
Okay.

291
00:24:09,115 --> 00:24:10,864
Mom.

292
00:24:18,625 --> 00:24:20,865
Joyce...

293
00:24:30,737 --> 00:24:32,787
Thank you.

294
00:24:34,974 --> 00:24:35,975
Thank you.

295
00:24:35,975 --> 00:24:38,998
Mom, I believe it now.

296
00:24:40,747 --> 00:24:46,086
I now believe what you saw...

297
00:24:46,086 --> 00:24:47,721
what Liam was saying...

298
00:24:47,721 --> 00:24:50,849
I now believe what I saw
in my dreams, mom.

299
00:24:54,227 --> 00:24:55,995
Thank you.

300
00:24:55,995 --> 00:24:59,634
It's so nice to hear you call me "Mom".

301
00:25:01,857 --> 00:25:07,655
I'm sure Liam will be glad.

302
00:25:09,112 --> 00:25:11,827
I wish he was here.

303
00:25:14,714 --> 00:25:17,507
Don't worry.

304
00:25:19,719 --> 00:25:21,999
I will take care of it.

305
00:25:26,693 --> 00:25:30,730
What do you mean by that?

306
00:25:30,730 --> 00:25:35,367
You're making me nervous, Joyce.

307
00:25:37,103 --> 00:25:39,394
Joyce...

308
00:26:01,728 --> 00:26:03,396
Intoy.

309
00:26:03,396 --> 00:26:05,432
Intoy, I'm now convinced.

310
00:26:05,432 --> 00:26:08,802
I now believe what you and Liam told me.

311
00:26:08,802 --> 00:26:12,974
I now believe that the typewriter is magical.

312
00:26:14,407 --> 00:26:16,075
I saw my past life.

313
00:26:16,075 --> 00:26:20,180
I saw my previous life with Liam.

314
00:26:20,180 --> 00:26:24,317
Our life with our son, Dex.

315
00:26:24,317 --> 00:26:29,350
I saw how Liam used the typewriter
to change everything.

316
00:26:32,898 --> 00:26:35,161
Joyce...

317
00:26:35,161 --> 00:26:37,731
Do you know where the typewriter is?

318
00:26:38,765 --> 00:26:41,091
Lando took it from me.

319
00:26:42,669 --> 00:26:46,306
That typewriter is so powerful.

320
00:26:46,306 --> 00:26:49,542
It's dangerous that it is in the wrong hands.

321
00:26:49,542 --> 00:26:53,112
I saw Via use it.

322
00:26:53,112 --> 00:26:55,281
I saw how she used it
to bring Liam back to life.

323
00:26:55,281 --> 00:26:56,783
I saw it...

324
00:26:56,783 --> 00:26:59,041
But I wasn't able to get it.

325
00:27:00,687 --> 00:27:03,223
The typewriter was left at Pulang Buhangin.

326
00:27:03,223 --> 00:27:05,892
What if someone else takes it?

327
00:27:05,892 --> 00:27:08,155
How can we get it?

328
00:27:09,329 --> 00:27:10,697
What?

329
00:27:11,798 --> 00:27:13,800
You can't leave this place anymore.

330
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:15,485
But I can.

331
00:27:29,582 --> 00:27:34,487
In the name of Dior, Gucci,
and holy Versace...

332
00:27:34,487 --> 00:27:36,422
Please take care of me.

333
00:27:37,423 --> 00:27:38,725
Okay.

334
00:27:46,666 --> 00:27:49,033
Aren't you Via's assistant?

335
00:27:51,404 --> 00:27:53,400
What are you doing here?

336
00:27:55,742 --> 00:27:56,900
Me?

337
00:27:57,744 --> 00:27:59,846
What am I doing here?

338
00:28:00,914 --> 00:28:02,682
That's what I ask myself, too.

339
00:28:02,682 --> 00:28:05,251
What am I doing here?

340
00:28:05,251 --> 00:28:07,650
Looks like I have an existential crisis.

341
00:28:08,354 --> 00:28:10,023
Tell me the truth.

342
00:28:10,023 --> 00:28:11,457
What?

343
00:28:11,457 --> 00:28:13,947
You're spying on us, aren't you?

344
00:28:15,194 --> 00:28:17,363
Where's Via?

345
00:28:17,363 --> 00:28:19,032
Where's Liam?

346
00:28:19,032 --> 00:28:20,763
Miss Via?

347
00:28:21,634 --> 00:28:23,536
Who is Via?

348
00:28:23,536 --> 00:28:26,439
Don't make me force you.

349
00:28:26,439 --> 00:28:29,242
You want the easy way or the hard way?

350
00:28:29,242 --> 00:28:31,244
Tell me where they are.

351
00:28:32,879 --> 00:28:34,780
Miss Via.

352
00:28:34,780 --> 00:28:36,149
That Via.

353
00:28:36,149 --> 00:28:38,983
Of course! She's at...

354
00:28:38,983 --> 00:28:41,154
At...

355
00:28:41,154 --> 00:28:42,755
Look over there!

356
00:28:44,591 --> 00:28:45,998
Hey!

357
00:28:58,404 --> 00:29:04,142
Your life got ruined because of me...

358
00:29:13,388 --> 00:29:14,869
Via...

359
00:29:19,292 --> 00:29:21,616
You don't deserve me, Via.

360
00:29:24,764 --> 00:29:26,819
I'll be honest with you.

361
00:29:28,868 --> 00:29:34,029
I got mad for what you did to me...

362
00:29:36,776 --> 00:29:39,189
For what you and Joyce did.

363
00:29:41,381 --> 00:29:43,786
You don't know the date today, do you?

364
00:29:45,852 --> 00:29:48,330
Eight years ago today...

365
00:29:50,056 --> 00:29:52,355
We met on that bridge.

366
00:30:00,733 --> 00:30:04,709
Liam, tell me.

367
00:30:05,638 --> 00:30:10,346
That day, should I have just
jumped off the bridge?

368
00:30:11,544 --> 00:30:14,981
So I wouldn't be hurting like this?

369
00:30:14,981 --> 00:30:17,457
That's what you're telling me right now.

370
00:30:18,584 --> 00:30:21,921
That I shouldn't have met you
because if we didn't meet,

371
00:30:21,921 --> 00:30:26,081
our life wouldn't be this messy.

372
00:30:26,926 --> 00:30:29,745
A year before that day,

373
00:30:32,746 --> 00:30:36,799
my mom took her own life.

374
00:30:38,274 --> 00:30:41,267
My mom killed herself, Liam.

375
00:30:43,676 --> 00:30:47,213
I came to a point...

376
00:30:47,213 --> 00:30:49,441
where I wished...

377
00:30:50,917 --> 00:30:53,496
to die.

378
00:30:54,687 --> 00:30:56,522
I wanted to die, too.

379
00:30:56,522 --> 00:30:58,160
Via...

380
00:30:59,592 --> 00:31:02,090
Until I met you.

381
00:31:09,602 --> 00:31:15,511
You made me feel that
I still deserve to be loved...

382
00:31:18,411 --> 00:31:22,215
That I still have a purpose to live.

383
00:31:22,215 --> 00:31:26,085
That's why it hurts so much, Liam.

384
00:31:26,085 --> 00:31:37,063
The reason I'm living
is also the reason I'm slowly dying.

385
00:31:37,063 --> 00:31:40,633
Now you're telling me
that you should have died?

386
00:31:40,633 --> 00:31:42,902
That's so selfish, Liam.

387
00:31:42,902 --> 00:31:44,937
You're being selfish.

388
00:31:44,937 --> 00:31:46,939
Via, I'm sorry.

389
00:31:46,939 --> 00:31:48,566
I'm sorry.

390
00:31:51,811 --> 00:31:53,808
Don't worry.

391
00:31:55,248 --> 00:31:59,188
All your suffering will end.

392
00:32:01,487 --> 00:32:03,956
I'll get better.

393
00:32:03,956 --> 00:32:06,352
And then, you can leave me.

394
00:32:29,516 --> 00:32:31,463
Go eat.

395
00:32:33,899 --> 00:32:36,591
Love is not perfect, Via.

396
00:32:39,298 --> 00:32:41,192
What do you mean?

397
00:32:45,065 --> 00:32:47,068
It's not always right.

398
00:32:48,969 --> 00:32:57,161
That's why we make mistakes because of love.

399
00:32:58,946 --> 00:33:01,349
But at the end of the day,

400
00:33:03,650 --> 00:33:09,990
one must be brave enough
to correct all those mistakes...

401
00:33:09,990 --> 00:33:12,456
still for love.

402
00:33:14,194 --> 00:33:16,245
Still...

403
00:33:18,632 --> 00:33:21,884
love is an act of bravery.

404
00:33:23,036 --> 00:33:24,658
You're right.

405
00:33:59,039 --> 00:34:04,878
<i>You're such a stupid, stupid,
pretty rich girl, Via.</i>

406
00:34:04,878 --> 00:34:09,095
<i>Chasing after a guy who obviously
doesn't love you.</i>

407
00:34:13,478 --> 00:34:19,526
<i>Trapped in a wheelchair, lost in the woods.</i>

408
00:34:19,526 --> 00:34:21,455
<i>Wake up.</i>

409
00:34:24,898 --> 00:34:27,067
<i>The things we do for love.</i>

410
00:34:27,067 --> 00:34:33,157
<i>As you say, love is an act of bravery.</i>

411
00:34:46,620 --> 00:34:49,339
I hope I'm not interrupting.

412
00:34:50,557 --> 00:34:54,094
<i>Did you already find the typewriter, Dad?</i>

413
00:34:54,094 --> 00:34:56,467
You really are my daughter.

414
00:34:57,798 --> 00:35:01,038
I'm not surprised that you're still alive.

415
00:35:02,436 --> 00:35:05,372
<i>You called from a faraway land</i>

416
00:35:05,372 --> 00:35:10,043
just to ask about the typewriter.

417
00:35:10,043 --> 00:35:12,446
Ridiculous.

418
00:35:12,446 --> 00:35:16,250
Won't a laptop suffice, Via?

419
00:35:16,250 --> 00:35:19,620
<i>Can you be serious, Dad?</i>

420
00:35:19,620 --> 00:35:24,925
Don't forget that you did me wrong.

421
00:35:24,925 --> 00:35:26,958
You shot me.

422
00:35:26,958 --> 00:35:30,664
Who was stupid enough to take the bullet?

423
00:35:30,664 --> 00:35:32,369
<i>Don't be rude.</i>

424
00:35:33,467 --> 00:35:37,337
I found a way to stop Liam
from messing with you.

425
00:35:37,337 --> 00:35:40,641
<i>I'm not as stupid as you think.</i>

426
00:35:40,641 --> 00:35:45,445
You did that for your own selfish reason.

427
00:35:45,445 --> 00:35:47,444
<i>Where are you?</i>

428
00:35:48,348 --> 00:35:52,486
I'm also not that stupid, Dad.

429
00:35:52,486 --> 00:35:54,855
Why would I tell you?

430
00:35:54,855 --> 00:35:57,351
<i>You'll kill Liam.</i>

431
00:35:59,491 --> 00:36:01,288
Did you find it?

432
00:36:04,765 --> 00:36:06,533
Who's that?

433
00:36:06,533 --> 00:36:08,368
Did they find the typewriter?

434
00:36:08,368 --> 00:36:10,804
Not yet!

435
00:36:10,804 --> 00:36:14,130
You have really gone insane!

436
00:36:15,142 --> 00:36:17,755
Who did I take after?

437
00:36:42,903 --> 00:36:46,239
Find the typewriter, Dad.

438
00:36:46,239 --> 00:36:51,244
I will tell you where to bring and leave it.

439
00:36:51,244 --> 00:36:55,549
<i>I will tell you where we are
once you find it.</i>

440
00:36:55,549 --> 00:36:57,184
What kind of game is this?

441
00:36:57,184 --> 00:36:59,519
<i>Find the typewriter.</i>

442
00:36:59,519 --> 00:37:02,089
I need to find it!

443
00:37:02,089 --> 00:37:04,466
Where are you and Liam?

444
00:37:23,910 --> 00:37:27,147
It's not enough
that I brought you back to life, Liam.

445
00:37:29,282 --> 00:37:32,586
I will find a way...

446
00:37:32,586 --> 00:37:35,731
to take Joyce out of your life.

447
00:37:52,205 --> 00:37:53,701
Via.

448
00:37:55,008 --> 00:37:56,910
Via!

449
00:37:56,910 --> 00:37:59,131
Why didn't you wake me up?

450
00:38:00,414 --> 00:38:01,990
Careful.

451
00:38:02,883 --> 00:38:04,600
Okay.

452
00:38:06,006 --> 00:38:07,807
What happened?

453
00:38:08,922 --> 00:38:13,260
I tried to wake you up because
I needed to use the bathroom.

454
00:38:13,260 --> 00:38:15,095
But I fell.

455
00:38:17,798 --> 00:38:19,900
Sorry, did I wake you up?

456
00:38:19,900 --> 00:38:23,396
No, but you had me worried.

457
00:38:24,871 --> 00:38:26,446
Sorry.

458
00:38:42,155 --> 00:38:44,740
Oh, ouch! Ouch!

459
00:38:47,427 --> 00:38:50,964
Bro, please watch where you're going.

460
00:38:50,964 --> 00:38:53,767
You're gross.

461
00:38:53,767 --> 00:38:56,269
Gross? Wow.

462
00:38:56,269 --> 00:38:58,171
You think you're so handsome?

463
00:38:58,171 --> 00:39:00,826
I'm sorry. I was just surprised.

464
00:39:04,945 --> 00:39:06,646
Bro...

465
00:39:06,646 --> 00:39:10,117
Do you have food with you?

466
00:39:10,117 --> 00:39:12,916
I haven't eaten since dinner.

467
00:39:13,787 --> 00:39:15,730
So, midnight snack?

468
00:39:15,730 --> 00:39:17,658
You haven't had your midnight snack?

469
00:39:18,625 --> 00:39:20,827
What's that?

470
00:39:20,827 --> 00:39:22,195
My stomach hurts already.

471
00:39:22,195 --> 00:39:24,088
It's rumbling.

472
00:39:26,466 --> 00:39:28,564
Like that, and then...

473
00:39:30,303 --> 00:39:32,172
Bro, look at me.

474
00:39:32,172 --> 00:39:34,875
What are you looking for?

475
00:39:34,875 --> 00:39:36,619
Nothing.

476
00:39:40,647 --> 00:39:43,849
That's how life is, bro.

477
00:39:45,318 --> 00:39:49,723
We search for things that are...

478
00:39:49,723 --> 00:39:51,335
already gone.

479
00:39:52,325 --> 00:40:02,002
Most of the time,
we lose some things because of our choices.

480
00:40:03,570 --> 00:40:05,172
You're just hungry.

481
00:40:05,172 --> 00:40:06,506
- Here.
- Bro.

482
00:40:06,506 --> 00:40:08,941
Get some midnight snack.

483
00:40:09,676 --> 00:40:11,077
Wait, I don't have...

484
00:40:11,077 --> 00:40:13,522
Bro, can I have it?

485
00:40:16,716 --> 00:40:18,827
- Go on.
- Bro...

486
00:40:23,690 --> 00:40:25,559
Thank you.

487
00:40:25,559 --> 00:40:27,761
Thank you for this, bro.

488
00:40:27,761 --> 00:40:30,330
This means a lot.

489
00:40:30,330 --> 00:40:33,300
This means a lot.
But don't you ever steal my stuff.

490
00:40:33,300 --> 00:40:35,435
- They're mine...
- I don't have any intentions.

491
00:40:35,435 --> 00:40:37,204
I'll just count this to see what it can buy...

492
00:40:37,204 --> 00:40:38,877
Go on.

493
00:40:41,241 --> 00:40:44,416
Popcorn and lechon.

494
00:41:09,736 --> 00:41:11,071
Facing both charges,

495
00:41:11,071 --> 00:41:15,909
former Congressman Ramon dela Peña
remains at large,

496
00:41:15,909 --> 00:41:24,918
but we won't stop until we find him.

497
00:41:24,918 --> 00:41:28,722
<i>Evidence gathered shows that Ramon dela Peña</i>

498
00:41:28,722 --> 00:41:34,127
<i>is behind the death of his former personnel,
Lando Nakpil.</i>

499
00:41:34,127 --> 00:41:38,098
We encourage the public to inform the police

500
00:41:38,098 --> 00:41:46,773
<i>if they have information
that can help our search.</i>

501
00:41:46,773 --> 00:41:49,943
<i>Because this man is extremely dangerous.</i>

502
00:41:49,943 --> 00:41:53,079
I knew it! We're not safe here!

503
00:41:56,283 --> 00:42:00,845
<i>And to you, Ramon dela Peña,
your days are numbered.</i>

504
00:42:11,831 --> 00:42:14,167
Sir, we already found him.

505
00:42:14,167 --> 00:42:15,802
Did you find Liam?

506
00:42:15,802 --> 00:42:19,372
- No.
- Darn it! What did you find?

507
00:42:19,372 --> 00:42:21,379
The warehouse.

508
00:42:27,814 --> 00:42:31,351
Here are the toiletries that you requested.

509
00:42:32,519 --> 00:42:34,154
You need it more...

510
00:42:34,154 --> 00:42:36,656
To clean up your son's name!

511
00:42:36,656 --> 00:42:38,692
You're way out of line.

512
00:42:38,692 --> 00:42:41,328
Can't you be a little considerate?

513
00:42:41,328 --> 00:42:44,497
I don't even know where my son is,
or if he's okay.

514
00:42:44,497 --> 00:42:46,700
Don't you have mercy?

515
00:42:46,700 --> 00:42:48,802
Why would I have mercy?

516
00:42:48,802 --> 00:42:51,471
Whatever happens to him,
your son deserves it!

517
00:42:51,471 --> 00:42:52,739
I don't even care about him!

518
00:42:52,739 --> 00:42:55,437
He deserves whatever will happen to him!

519
00:42:55,437 --> 00:42:56,710
- Mom!
- You're so mean!

520
00:42:56,710 --> 00:42:58,011
Take back what you said!

521
00:42:58,011 --> 00:42:59,212
- Take it back!
- No!

522
00:42:59,212 --> 00:43:01,081
Take it back! My son is not a bad person!

523
00:43:01,081 --> 00:43:02,182
- Madam, that's enough.
- Mom!

524
00:43:02,182 --> 00:43:03,583
Please!

525
00:43:03,583 --> 00:43:05,485
Please.

526
00:43:05,485 --> 00:43:10,013
Fighting won't do any good!

527
00:43:11,358 --> 00:43:14,361
Dad is right, Mom.

528
00:43:14,361 --> 00:43:19,881
We should not waste our energy
in useless fights like this.

529
00:43:20,867 --> 00:43:24,070
We all want one thing.
For all of us to be safe.

530
00:43:24,070 --> 00:43:25,905
That's it!

531
00:43:25,905 --> 00:43:28,574
Mommy, please listen.

532
00:43:29,442 --> 00:43:33,361
No one will die if you cooperate.

533
00:43:34,881 --> 00:43:37,792
Just this once, Mom. Please.

534
00:43:39,219 --> 00:43:41,187
Suit yourself.

535
00:43:41,187 --> 00:43:43,022
Joanne.

536
00:43:47,127 --> 00:43:48,795
- Dad.
- No.

537
00:43:48,795 --> 00:43:50,387
I got it.

538
00:43:56,903 --> 00:43:59,095
Mom, I'm sorry.

539
00:44:06,880 --> 00:44:08,564
Joanne!

540
00:44:10,450 --> 00:44:12,485
Joanne, I'm blind. Where are you?

541
00:44:12,485 --> 00:44:14,587
I'm not here.

542
00:44:19,626 --> 00:44:20,660
Joanne...

543
00:44:20,660 --> 00:44:24,441
Did you follow me here to lecture me, too?

544
00:44:25,265 --> 00:44:28,234
Then do the same thing to me.

545
00:44:28,234 --> 00:44:32,472
We both have shortcomings as parents.

546
00:44:32,472 --> 00:44:37,277
If only I didn't get addicted to drugs...

547
00:44:37,277 --> 00:44:42,255
If only I had prioritized your needs first...

548
00:44:44,184 --> 00:44:48,005
I wasn't a good husband to you, Joanne.

549
00:44:49,289 --> 00:44:52,583
I hope someday you can forgive me.

550
00:44:55,295 --> 00:44:57,611
I feel bad that...

551
00:44:58,798 --> 00:45:01,868
I'm now blind.

552
00:45:01,868 --> 00:45:03,937
But God knows...

553
00:45:03,937 --> 00:45:11,937
God knows how much I want
to hug my wife and daughter.

554
00:45:17,784 --> 00:45:19,941
I still love you, Jo.

555
00:45:20,887 --> 00:45:22,714
Nothing has changed.

556
00:45:24,130 --> 00:45:30,917
I lost my sight,
but my love for you and Joyce remains.

557
00:45:33,666 --> 00:45:36,703
I'm scared.

558
00:45:36,703 --> 00:45:43,009
I'm scared of what can happen
to our daughter, Edmond.

559
00:45:43,009 --> 00:45:45,078
Nothing bad will happen, Joanne.

560
00:45:45,078 --> 00:45:46,986
We're strong.

561
00:45:48,147 --> 00:45:50,183
Let's work together.

562
00:45:56,721 --> 00:45:58,560
Lord...

563
00:46:01,261 --> 00:46:04,800
I don't know what's happening to my son.

564
00:46:08,201 --> 00:46:12,972
I also don't know where he is.

565
00:46:18,044 --> 00:46:21,592
I hope my son is okay wherever he is.

566
00:46:22,582 --> 00:46:24,209
Tess.

567
00:46:30,290 --> 00:46:33,860
Lord, Lord...

568
00:46:33,860 --> 00:46:40,233
I want Liam to be here.

569
00:46:40,233 --> 00:46:42,969
Why did you send this man?

570
00:46:42,969 --> 00:46:47,707
You could have sent a guardian angel instead.

571
00:46:47,707 --> 00:46:49,114
Why?

572
00:46:52,378 --> 00:46:57,473
I'll add security here to watch over you.

573
00:46:59,485 --> 00:47:02,889
Danilo, don't worry about me.

574
00:47:02,889 --> 00:47:05,425
Find Liam.

575
00:47:05,425 --> 00:47:08,595
I also hired a private investigator.

576
00:47:08,595 --> 00:47:11,664
He's already moving.

577
00:47:11,664 --> 00:47:15,435
I'm just being careful
because I don't want Ramon

578
00:47:15,435 --> 00:47:17,983
to trace Liam through me.

579
00:47:20,506 --> 00:47:25,011
Promise me that our son
will come home to me.

580
00:47:25,011 --> 00:47:27,840
That Liam will be fine.

581
00:47:30,116 --> 00:47:31,655
Tess...

582
00:47:32,685 --> 00:47:35,825
I wasn't able to fight for you before.

583
00:47:36,789 --> 00:47:43,371
Now, I will do everything
to protect you and Liam.

584
00:47:44,297 --> 00:47:46,121
Forgive me.

585
00:47:47,834 --> 00:47:50,661
I wasn't as brave as your son.

586
00:47:54,540 --> 00:47:56,309
You know what...

587
00:47:57,443 --> 00:48:00,239
Liam isn't just brave.

588
00:48:01,814 --> 00:48:04,411
He's also kind-hearted.

589
00:48:06,386 --> 00:48:09,517
He taught me...

590
00:48:11,653 --> 00:48:16,829
that we don't have to stay in the dark.

591
00:48:16,829 --> 00:48:20,331
We can always choose the good thing.

592
00:48:22,068 --> 00:48:28,370
Danilo, whatever happened between us
in the past...

593
00:48:32,311 --> 00:48:34,651
I forgive you.

594
00:48:36,553 --> 00:48:37,750
Oh, no!

595
00:48:37,750 --> 00:48:39,018
No!

596
00:48:39,018 --> 00:48:40,420
Hard no!

597
00:48:40,420 --> 00:48:42,689
No!

598
00:48:42,689 --> 00:48:44,223
You.

599
00:48:44,223 --> 00:48:48,161
Looks like you want to take advantage.

600
00:48:48,161 --> 00:48:49,395
We're okay now.

601
00:48:49,395 --> 00:48:51,272
Tess, thank you.

602
00:48:53,389 --> 00:48:56,241
Thank you too, for everything, Danilo.

603
00:49:10,783 --> 00:49:13,992
- I love you so much.
- Mom, I love you so much.

604
00:49:13,992 --> 00:49:18,180
<i>If a couple loves each other,
they will face problems together.</i>

605
00:49:18,180 --> 00:49:20,361
<i>I wish I didn't let anger
get the better of me.</i>

606
00:49:20,361 --> 00:49:23,464
<i>I wish we had dealt with our problem
with Dex together.</i>

607
00:49:23,464 --> 00:49:25,099
I love you so much, Joyce.

608
00:49:25,099 --> 00:49:27,668
I love you so much, Liam.

609
00:49:27,668 --> 00:49:31,030
Let's go back to our old life.

610
00:49:36,147 --> 00:49:38,276
<i>Dex, my son...</i>

611
00:49:38,276 --> 00:49:41,580
<i>Mom's already in Paris.</i>

612
00:49:41,580 --> 00:49:44,282
<i>I've fulfilled my lifelong dream.</i>

613
00:49:44,282 --> 00:49:49,851
<i>Too bad, your dad and I
didn't fulfill it together.</i>
